      "writtenOn": "2024-10-18T20:16:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The `CMakeLists.txt` file is generated by `gn/gn_to_cmake.py`, like as stated at https://skia.org/docs/user/build/#cmake . However, note that this converter was mostly designed around allowing one to use an IDE which uses CMake as its native project management; it is not really designed to be used to build Skia \"for real\". Especially when it comes to complex builds like raster pipeline.\n\nDoes the build only fail when building with CMake (does building with gcc for loong using the normal gn/ninja build work)? Which version of gcc? If we\u0027re going to take changes like Skia is going to want to add at least a gcc loong builder (Skia does have gcc x86 and gcc x86_64 builders already).",
      "parentUuid": "43d8f211_92d1929a",
      "revId": "f097950730ec86d37b5599e9fbfc75b46a991420",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
